.TH QSAFE 1 "2026" "Qsafe 8.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qsafe \- hybrid post-quantum file encryption and signing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qsafe
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ input ]
.RI [ output ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qsafe
encrypts files using a hybrid key-establishment scheme that combines the
classical
.B X25519
Diffie\-Hellman exchange with the post\-quantum
.B ML\-KEM\-1024
(NIST FIPS 203) key encapsulation mechanism. The resulting shared secrets are
combined with HKDF\-SHA256 and used to wrap a random content key that protects
the payload with
.BR AES\-256\-GCM .
A file therefore stays confidential unless an attacker breaks
.I both
the classical and the post\-quantum layer.
.PP
Secret keys are stored on disk wrapped with a key derived from a passphrase
using the memory\-hard
.B scrypt
KDF. Encrypted files preserve the original name, permission bits and
modification time, and may be addressed to multiple recipients at once.
.PP
.B qsafe
can also create and verify detached
.B ML\-DSA\-87
(Dilithium, Level 5) signatures.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B keygen
Generate a hybrid X25519 + ML\-KEM\-1024 keypair. Run once.
.TP
.B encrypt " " \fIinput\fR " " [\fIoutput\fR]
Encrypt a file or directory to one or more public keys.
.TP
.B decrypt " " \fIinput\fR " " [\fIoutput\fR]
Decrypt a file or directory using the secret key.
.TP
.B verify " " \fIinput\fR
Authenticate an encrypted file or directory without writing any plaintext.
.TP
.B rekey
Change the passphrase that protects a secret key, without regenerating it.
.TP
.B inspect " " \fIfile\fR
Report what a key or encrypted file is, without decrypting it.
.TP
.B sign-keygen
Generate an ML\-DSA\-87 signing keypair.
.TP
.B sign " " \fIinput\fR " " [\fIsignature\fR]
Create a detached signature for a file (default \fIinput\fR.sig).
.TP
.B verify-sig " " \fIinput\fR " " [\fIsignature\fR]
Verify a detached signature against a file.
.TP
.B keys " " <list|path|import|remove>
Manage the keyring under ~/.qsafe (named identities and recipients).
.TP
.B split-key " " [\fIprefix\fR]
Split the secret key into \fB\-\-shares\fR Shamir shares over GF(256), any
\fB\-\-threshold\fR of which reconstruct it. Each share file is unencrypted
key material \(em store them separately.
.TP
.B join-key " " \fIshare\fR " " \fIshare\fR " " [\fIshare\fR...]
Reconstruct a secret key from shares and re\-wrap it under a freshly
confirmed passphrase.
.TP
.B age-keygen / age-encrypt / age-decrypt
Interoperate with the classical age (X25519) v1 file format. For
\fIpost\-quantum\fR age recipients, see
.BR age-plugin-qsafe .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-key\-file " path"
Secret key file (default: secret_key.bin; sign_key.bin for signing commands).
.TP
.BI \-\-pub\-file " path"
Public key file (default: <key\-file>.pub).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recipient " " \fIpath\fR
Add a recipient public key when encrypting. May be given multiple times.
.TP
.BI \-\-passphrase " str"
Passphrase on the command line (discouraged; visible to other users).
.TP
.BI \-\-passphrase\-file " path"
Read the passphrase from the first line of a file.
.TP
.B \-\-check
For decrypt/verify: authenticate only, write no plaintext.
.TP
.BI \-\-sign\-with " sk"
For encrypt: embed an ML\-DSA\-87 sender signature inside the encrypted
payload (needs \fIsk\fR and \fIsk\fR.pub, from \fBsign-keygen\fR). Decrypt
verifies it automatically and reports the signer's fingerprint; verification
failure removes any output.
.TP
.BI \-\-signer " pk"
For decrypt/verify: additionally require the embedded signer to be exactly
this public key.
.TP
.B \-\-pad
For encrypt: append random padding to the file's Padm\('e bucket, so the
ciphertext length reveals only a coarse size class. Requires a regular file
input.
.TP
.BI \-\-threshold " t"
For split-key: shares needed to reconstruct (2\-16).
.TP
.BI \-\-shares " n"
For split-key: total shares to create (t\-255).
.TP
.B \-\-keychain
Store (key\-creating commands) or retrieve the wrapping passphrase in the OS
keychain \(em macOS Keychain or Windows DPAPI.
.TP
.BI \-\-identity " name"
Use (or, for keygen, create) a keyring identity under ~/.qsafe.
.TP
.B \-\-armor
Encrypt to ASCII base64 text; decrypt from base64 text.
.TP
.BI \-\-scrypt\-cost " n"
scrypt cost as log2(N), 14\-22 (default 15), used by keygen/rekey.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite output files without prompting.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QSAFE_PASSPHRASE
If set, used as the passphrase when none is given on the command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Generate a keypair, then encrypt and decrypt a file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
qsafe keygen
qsafe encrypt report.pdf
qsafe decrypt report.pdf.qsafe
.fi
.RE
.PP
Encrypt to two recipients:
.PP
.RS
.nf
qsafe encrypt -r alice.pub -r bob.pub secret.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sign and verify a release artifact:
.PP
.RS
.nf
qsafe sign-keygen
qsafe sign release.tar.gz
qsafe verify-sig release.tar.gz release.tar.gz.sig
.fi
.RE
.PP
Encrypt with an embedded sender signature and size hiding:
.PP
.RS
.nf
qsafe encrypt --sign-with sign_key.bin --pad -r alice.pub report.pdf
.fi
.RE
.PP
Split the secret key 2\-of\-3 and later recover it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
qsafe split-key --threshold 2 --shares 3 backup
qsafe join-key backup.share1 backup.share3
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B qsafe
exits 0 on success and non\-zero on error (including failed authentication or
signature verification).
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation in README.md.
